FAQ section: Module 4: Analytics Engineering with dbt
FAQ question: DBT: Why changing the target schema to “marts” actually creates a schema named “dbt_marts” instead?

Document (the answer, with line numbers):
1: It is a default behavior of dbt to [append custom schema to the initial schema](https://docs.getdbt.com/docs/build/custom-schemas#why-does-dbt-concatenate-the-custom-schema-to-the-target-schema). To override this behavior, create a macro named `generate_schema_name.sql`:
2: 
3: ```sql
4: {% macro generate_schema_name(custom_schema_name, node) -%}
5: 
6: {%- set default_schema = target.schema -%}
7: 
8: {%- if custom_schema_name is none -%}
9: 
10: {{ default_schema }}
11: 
12: {%- else -%}
13: 
14: {{ custom_schema_name | trim }}
15: 
16: {%- endif -%}
17: 
18: {%- endmacro %}
19: ```
20: 
21: Now you can override the default custom schema in `dbt_project.yml`.
